    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the reports!</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"300245\">@Filippo A. E. Nuccio</span>  In your case, it's because I fell for the classic blunder of case sensitivity (azure is case sensitive but GitHub isn't with the repo names). <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40766\">#40766</a> will fix this. I will also move all the affected blobs manually after this is merged to back-port the history.</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110050\">@Sébastien Gouëzel</span> In your case it was a similarly natured blunder of forgetting about Windows. Indeed it only means noise (it will download successfully after complaining). Here's the fix (plus an added Windows validation for good measure) <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40767\">#40767</a></p>",
        "id": 604591514,
        "sender_full_name": "Marcelo Lynch",
        "timestamp": 1781800368
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here is another report for an unexpected <code>cache</code> behavior. I have somehow a corrupt cache, so I tried redownloading everything, with <code>cache get!</code>. Here is the output:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">PS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"n\">Users</span><span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"n\">Sebastien</span><span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"n\">Desktop</span><span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"n\">mathlib4SG</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lake</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cache</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">get!</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Current</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">branch</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">avoid</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">ismanifold</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cache</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">https</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"n\">github</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">com</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">grunweg</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">mathlib4</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">git</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grunweg</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">mathlib4</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Attempting</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">download</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">8570</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grunweg</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">mathlib4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cache</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">https</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"n\">lakecache</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">blob</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">windows</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">net</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">mathlib4</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">master</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Downloaded</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">8449</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">attempted</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">8570</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"mi\">8570</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">592</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">KB</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Decompressed</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">8071</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Decompressed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">8449</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Decompressing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">8570</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">file</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Decompressed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">65424</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ms</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Completed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">successfully!</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>As you can see, it tried redownloading everything first from master, found some files but not all of them, but then instead of redownloading the missing files from the other cache source, it just used the ones that are already on my computer. So the corrupt cache was not fixed.</p>",
        "id": 604928048,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1781884277
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oops, yes, that's a bug introduced by the multi-layer fecthes. <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40817\">#40817</a></p>",
